Subject: [SE3-P6] mfplat: close the category key after enumerating transforms

mft_collect_machine_reg() opened the registry key of the requested MFT
category, enumerated its subkeys and returned without closing it, so every
MFTEnum/MFTEnumEx/MFTEnum2 lookup in the machine registry leaked one key
handle. The media engine looks up about five categories each time it opens
a video and the source reader about three, so a player that is created and
destroyed repeatedly kept accumulating handles (5 per open/close cycle in a
100-cycle loop, on vanilla GE-Proton11-11 as well). Close the key once the
enumeration is done.

---
diff --git a/dlls/mfplat/main.c b/dlls/mfplat/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfplat/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfplat/main.c
@@ -1257,6 +1257,7 @@
         index++;
     }
 
+    RegCloseKey(hlist);
     return S_OK;
 }
 
